.TH GIT-WTCLONE 1 2026-10-21 dotfiles "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-wtclone \- clone a repository into the bare worktree layout
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git wtclone
.RI [ "clone options" ]
.I repo
.RI [ dir ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clones
.I repo
the way
.BR git\-clone (1)
does, but lays it out so every worktree sits in one folder:
.PP
.RS
.nf
<dir>/.git        bare repository (git data only)
<dir>/<branch>    worktree of the checked-out branch
.fi
.RE
.PP
Worktrees that
.BR wt (1)
creates later land next to it as
.IR <dir>/<branch> .
The nono agent launchers grant the whole
.I <dir>
folder, so one agent session can work across all worktrees.
.PP
After cloning,
.B git wtclone
sets up the bare repository to behave like a normal clone:
.IP \(bu 2
remote branches are fetched as remote-tracking branches
.RI ( origin/* ),
and
.I origin/HEAD
points at the remote's default branch;
.IP \(bu 2
only the checked-out branch exists as a local branch, tracking its remote
branch;
.IP \(bu 2
submodules are initialized recursively in the new worktree.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I repo
The repository to clone, in any form
.BR git\-clone (1)
accepts.
.TP
.I dir
The container folder. Defaults to the last path component of
.I repo
without
.IR .git ,
created in the current folder. It must not exist or must be empty.
.SH OPTIONS
Options are passed on to
.BR git\-clone (1),
with these exceptions:
.TP
.BR \-\-bare ", " \-\-mirror ", " \-\-separate\-git\-dir
Rejected; they conflict with the layout.
.TP
.BR \-\-recurse\-submodules ", " \-\-recursive
Ignored; submodules are always initialized.
.TP
.BI \-b " branch"
Checks out
.I branch
instead of the remote's default branch. The worktree folder is named after it.
.TP
.B \-\-single\-branch
Fetches only the checked-out branch, now and on later fetches.
.SH FOLDER NAMES
Worktree folders use the branch name with
.B /
and
.B \e
replaced by
.BR \- ,
matching the
.B sanitize
filter of
.BR wt (1).
For example, branch
.I feature/login
becomes the folder
.IR feature\-login .
.SH CLASSIC REPOSITORIES
Repositories that must stay a regular clone, because another tool decides
where they live, keep working. For them,
.BR wt (1)
creates worktrees in a central folder instead:
.PP
.RS
.nf
~/.local/share/worktrees/<key>/<branch>
.fi
.RE
.PP
.I <key>
is the path of the main checkout with
.BR / ,
.BR \e ,
and
.B .
replaced by
.BR \- ,
for example
.I \-Users\-me\-\-local\-share\-chezmoi
for
.IR /Users/me/.local/share/chezmoi .
The nono agent launchers grant the main checkout and that folder.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git wtclone git@github.com:acme/foo.git
Creates
.I ./foo/.git
and
.I ./foo/main
(if
.I main
is the default branch).
.TP
.B git wtclone \-\-depth 1 git@github.com:acme/foo.git ~/projects/acme/foo
Shallow clone into
.IR ~/projects/acme/foo .
.TP
.B wt switch \-\-create feature/login
Run inside the container or a worktree afterwards; creates
.IR foo/feature\-login .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git\-wtmigrate (1),
.BR git\-clone (1),
.BR git\-worktree (1),
.BR wt (1)
